== What's New

=== DuckDB Replication
--
DuckDB database was added as a target-only replication platform.
Data can be loaded into DuckDB, but changes cannot be captured from it because DuckDB does not support triggers.

--

=== Java 25 Support
--
SymmetricDS now runs on Java 25 as well as Java 21. Java 21 is still the minimum required version, so existing installations do not need to change. The supported versions are Java 21 and Java 25, both long-term support releases.

The software is compiled for Java 21, so the same installation runs on either version. The official Docker images are now based on Java 25, including the SymmetricDS Pro hardened image, which uses the Java 25 JRE.

See also: <<System Requirements>>.
--

ifdef::pro[]

=== MotherDuck Support
--
SymmetricDS Pro can now replicate data into https://motherduck.com[MotherDuck], the cloud service for DuckDB, as a write-only target. Add MotherDuck with the Connect Database Wizard by selecting *MotherDuck* as the type. SymmetricDS connects with the DuckDB JDBC driver using a `jdbc:duckdb:md:<database>` URL and a MotherDuck access token.

Tables are created and altered in MotherDuck automatically, and data is loaded the same way as for a DuckDB target. Changes cannot be captured from MotherDuck.
--

=== Microsoft Fabric Warehouse Support
--
SymmetricDS Pro can now replicate data into a https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/data-warehouse/data-warehousing[Microsoft Fabric Warehouse] as a write-only target. Add the warehouse with the Configure Diagram or Connect Database Wizard by selecting *Microsoft Fabric Warehouse* as the type. The warehouse accepts only Microsoft Entra ID authentication, so SymmetricDS connects with the service principal of an Entra app registration.

A warehouse supports only a subset of SQL Server's data types and table definitions, so SymmetricDS adapts each table it creates or alters. Unsupported data types are converted to the closest supported type, and primary key, foreign key, and unique constraints are created with `NOT ENFORCED`, because a warehouse never enforces them. A change that a warehouse cannot apply to an existing column, such as making it required or shrinking it, is handled by rebuilding the table, with the existing rows backed up to a `<table>_` table while it runs.

Data is loaded with JDBC batch statements by default. When the tenant, workspace, and lakehouse IDs of a OneLake lakehouse are set, a bulk channel uploads each batch to the lakehouse and loads it with the `COPY INTO` statement, which is faster for large loads.
--

=== Microsoft Fabric SQL Database Support
--
SymmetricDS Pro can now replicate data both into and out of a https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/database/sql/overview[SQL database in Microsoft Fabric]. Add the database with the Configure Diagram or Connect Database Wizard by selecting *SQL Database in Microsoft Fabric* as the type. The database accepts only Microsoft Entra ID authentication, so SymmetricDS connects with the service principal of an Entra app registration.

Changes are captured with database triggers, which is the default capture type in the wizard. SymmetricDS creates insert, update, and delete triggers on the tables that are configured for capture. It does not capture the changes that it makes while it loads data, so two nodes can replicate in both directions. Changes to the structure of a table are captured when the `trigger.capture.ddl.changes` parameter is enabled, and a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric can be the source of a mirror that replicates both data and structure changes to SQL Server, SQL Server Azure, or another SQL database in Microsoft Fabric. See the user guide for the permissions that SymmetricDS needs and for the known limitations.

A bulk channel that loads a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric loads inserts with the bulk copy API of the Microsoft JDBC driver instead of JDBC batch statements. No additional configuration is needed.
--

endif::pro[]

=== ClickHouse Support
--
SymmetricDS can now load data into a https://clickhouse.com/[ClickHouse] database as a write-only target. Data from any other supported database can be inserted, updated, and deleted in ClickHouse tables. SymmetricDS creates missing tables as `MergeTree` tables, with the primary key as the sorting key, and applies added, modified, and dropped columns. Use `symadmin module install clickhouse` to install the JDBC driver.

ClickHouse always reports zero rows changed for an update or delete, so the loader treats them as successful and conflict detection does not work on this target. Capture, use as a source, a bulk loader, and ClickHouse Cloud are not supported. See <<ClickHouse>> for details.
--

=== Post-Quantum Key Exchange
--
On Java 25.0.5 and later, HTTPS connections between nodes use the hybrid TLS 1.3 key exchange groups `X25519MLKEM768`, `SecP256r1MLKEM768`, and `SecP384r1MLKEM1024`, which protect recorded traffic against future quantum computers. No configuration change is needed. When either side does not support a hybrid group, such as a node running Java 21, the connection falls back to a classical group and still succeeds.

ifdef::pro[]
For how to verify the negotiated group and how to restrict the groups, see link:user-guide.html#_post_quantum_key_exchange[Post-Quantum Key Exchange].
endif::pro[]
--
